:: UC1 {"position":"1100,600","size":"100,100"}
Customer service becomes overwhelmed as users complain about recent changes and request to downgrade. Many begin reverting to the previous version of the tool.

How do you respond?

<div style="text-align: center;">
<img src="https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1139617600/vector/angry-older-men-and-women-of-the-telephone-operator.jpg?s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=HbuTpfaBi8QmPfXQR4KOII97n0RIRx3WcjxUWZ2cyZY=" style="border-radius: 50%; width: 400px;">
</div>



[[Rollback all users to the old version->UC1.1]]

[[Continue supporting both the old and new versions->UC1.2]]


:: UC1.1 {"position":"1225,500","size":"100,100"}
Both shareholders and users are dissatisfied.

<div style="text-align: center;">
<img style="width:200px; height:200px;"
src="https://cdn-icons-png.flaticon.com/512/10130/10130489.png">
</div>

[[Next->UC1.1.1]]

<audio src="https://files.catbox.moe/vj85jh.mp3" autoplay></audio>


:: UC1.1.1 {"position":"1350,500","size":"100,100"}
The company accelerates development of the new version, while maintaining the old one continues to incur operational costs. However, by reverting to active development rather than ongoing operation, the company avoids additional expenses for the partially implemented new version.

<div style="text-align: center;">
<img style="width:250px; height:300px;"
src="https://cdn-icons-png.flaticon.com/512/10017/10017583.png">
</div>

[[Next->UC1.1.2]]


:: UC1.1.2 {"position":"1475,500","size":"100,100"}
Following the rollback to the older version and the delay of the new one, the company must determine how to best meet the needs of both users and stakeholders. With resources divided between maintaining the existing version and continuing development of the new version, leadership must now decide how to move forward.

<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; width: 100%;">
  <img style="width:200px; height:200px;" src="https://cdn-icons-png.flaticon.com/512/747/747685.png">
  <img style="width:200px; height:200px;" src="https://cdn-icons-png.flaticon.com/512/8443/8443368.png">
</div>


[[Next->UC1.1.3]]


:: UC1.1.3 {"position":"1600,500","size":"100,100"}
As a final measure, the development team is allocated additional budget to explore implementation options, aiming to determine what would best satisfy both stakeholders and users. After repeated back-and-forth discussions, only one viable path remains.

<div style="text-align: center;">
<img style="width:200px; height:200px;"
src="https://cdn-icons-png.flaticon.com/512/781/781831.png">
</div>

[[Consult users and stakeholders on improvements->UC1.1.4]]


:: UC1.1.4 {"position":"1725,500","size":"100,100"}
Both users and stakeholders are reasonably satisfied with the outcome, as feedback from both groups was incorporated into the tool’s development. Although minor flaws remain, they can be resolved over time. The company still incurs financial losses; however, because both parties are aligned, phasing out the older version becomes easier as they collectively adopt the new one.

<div style="text-align: center;">
<img style="width:200px; height:200px;"
src="https://cdn-icons-png.flaticon.com/512/12486/12486905.png">
</div>

<audio src="https://files.catbox.moe/m5nhdr.mp3" autoplay></audio>

